Description: Fits, simulates and checks spatial and spatio-temporal point
    process models on hyperrectangular domains of any dimension. The
    log-intensity of Poisson and marked Poisson processes can combine
    coordinates, scalar and functional covariates, categorical and continuous
    marks, and smooth terms, and is fitted by a multidimensional extension of
    the Berman-Turner device (Baddeley and Turner (2000)
    <doi:10.1111/1467-842X.00128>). The same intensity is the first-order
    component of log-Gaussian Cox processes (Moller et al. (1998)
    <doi:10.1111/1467-9469.00115>) and of epidemic-type aftershock sequence
    models (Ogata (1998) <doi:10.1023/A:1003403601725>) with regression-based
    background intensities. Multidimensional inhomogeneous K-functions,
    residuals and global envelope tests are provided for model checking. The
    ETAS triggering routine is adapted from the 'Fortran' code of the
    'etasFLP' package.
